---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Wash Your Shower Curtain in the Washing Machine — TestedByTom" description="No scrubbing, no chemicals, no effort. Throw it in the washing machine and go do something else.">
<style>
  main {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2.5rem 1.25rem 5rem;
  }

  .breadcrumb {
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 1.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
  }
  .breadcrumb a {
    color: var(--rust);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .breadcrumb a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .breadcrumb span { margin: 0 0.4rem; }

  .post-header {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    padding-bottom: 2rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .post-tag {
    display: inline-block;
    background: var(--rust);
    color: white;
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    padding: 0.25rem 0.65rem;
    border-radius: 2px;
    margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
  }
  .post-title {
    font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif;
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 4.5vw, 2.4rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--brown);
    line-height: 1.2;
    margin-bottom: 0.65rem;
  }
  .post-subtitle {
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-style: italic;
    font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .post-meta {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .post-body {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--brown);
  }
  .post-body p {
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .materials-box {
    background: var(--warm-white);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--tan);
    border-radius: 2px;
    padding: 1.5rem 1.75rem;
    margin: 2rem 0;
  }
  .materials-box h3 {
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--brown);
    margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
  }
  .materials-box ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
    color: var(--brown);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.9;
  }

  .steps-list {
    counter-reset: steps;
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 2rem;
  }
  .steps-list li {
    counter-increment: steps;
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
    align-items: flex-start;
  }
  .steps-list li::before {
    content: counter(steps);
    background: var(--rust);
    color: white;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    min-width: 1.6rem;
    height: 1.6rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    margin-top: 0.15rem;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .steps-list li p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.97rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--brown);
  }

  .callout {
    background: var(--cream);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--rust);
    border-radius: 2px;
    padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
    margin: 2rem 0;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--brown);
  }
  .callout strong {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--rust);
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
    font-family: 'Lato', sans-serif;
  }

  .rating-section {
    background: var(--warm-white);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 2px;
    padding: 1.75rem;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }
  .rating-label {
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--rust);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .rating-row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .rating-name {
    min-width: 120px;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .rating-stars { color: var(--rust); font-size: 0.85rem; }
  .rating-score { font-weight: 700; color: var(--brown); font-size: 0.85rem; }
  .rating-final {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding-top: 1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    margin: 1rem 0;
  }
  .final-label {
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .final-score {
    font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif;
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--rust);
  }
  .rating-notes {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: 1.6;
    font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .back-link {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: 3rem;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--rust);
    text-decoration: none;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
  }
  .back-link:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
</style>

<main>
  <div class="breadcrumb">
    <a href="/">Home</a><span>›</span>
    <a href="/household-tips">Household Tips</a><span>›</span>
    Wash Your Shower Curtain in the Washing Machine
  </div>

  <div class="post-header">
    <span class="post-tag">Household Tip · Bathroom</span>
    <h1 class="post-title">Wash Your Shower Curtain in the Washing Machine</h1>
    <p class="post-subtitle">No scrubbing, no chemicals, no effort. Throw it in and go do something else.</p>
    <div class="post-meta">Tested · Still doing it</div>
  </div>

  <div class="post-body">
    <p>Most people either scrub their shower curtain by hand or just throw it out when it gets gross enough. There's a better way and it takes about 30 seconds of actual effort on your part.</p>

    <p>Just wash it in the washing machine. That's it. That's the tip.</p>

    <div class="materials-box">
      <h3>What You Need</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>A washing machine</li>
        <li>Your regular laundry detergent</li>
        <li>A couple of towels (optional but helpful)</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <h2 style="font-family:'Playfair Display',serif;font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--brown);margin:2rem 0 1rem;">How to Do It</h2>

    <ol class="steps-list">
      <li><p>Take the curtain off the rings — you don't need to remove the rings themselves, just unhook the curtain.</p></li>
      <li><p>Throw it in the washing machine. Toss in a couple of bath towels if you have them — they act as scrubbers and help balance the load.</p></li>
      <li><p>Add your normal detergent. Regular cycle, warm water.</p></li>
      <li><p>When it's done, hang it back up on the rod to air dry. Don't put it in the dryer.</p></li>
    </ol>

    <div class="callout">
      <strong>Does it actually work?</strong>
      Yes. Soap scum, mildew, pink slime — all of it comes out. The curtain comes out looking close to new. The towels do a lot of the physical scrubbing work while it tumbles around.
    </div>

    <p>Check the curtain label first if you're worried — most fabric and plastic/PEVA curtains handle a machine wash fine on a gentle or regular cycle. If yours is some delicate specialty material, hand wash it. But the standard ones you get at any store? Machine wash them.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="rating-section">
    <div class="rating-label">Honest Rating</div>
    <div class="rating-row">
      <span class="rating-name">Ease</span>
      <span class="rating-stars">★★★★★</span>
      <span class="rating-score">5/5</span>
    </div>
    <div class="rating-row">
      <span class="rating-name">Effectiveness</span>
      <span class="rating-stars">★★★★★</span>
      <span class="rating-score">5/5</span>
    </div>
    <div class="rating-row">
      <span class="rating-name">Cleanup</span>
      <span class="rating-stars">★★★★★</span>
      <span class="rating-score">5/5</span>
    </div>
    <div class="rating-final">
      <span class="final-label">Final Score</span>
      <span class="final-score">5.00 / 5</span>
    </div>
    <p class="rating-notes">Zero effort, great results. I don't know why this isn't common knowledge. Stop scrubbing your shower curtain.</p>
  </div>

  <a href="/household-tips" class="back-link">← Back to Household Tips</a>
</main>
</Layout>
